WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.070
Charles Darwin and Alfred Russel
Wallace worked separately.

2
00:00:04.120 --> 00:00:05.930
Yet in eighteen fifty-eight,

3
00:00:05.980 --> 00:00:09.850
they shared the same big idea
with the world, together.

4
00:00:09.900 --> 00:00:13.370
A year later, Darwin published
a famous book about it,

5
00:00:13.420 --> 00:00:15.630
On the Origin of Species.

6
00:00:15.680 --> 00:00:19.890
Even so, many scientists
took years to be convinced.

7
00:00:19.940 --> 00:00:23.710
Why was such a big idea
so slow to be accepted?

8
00:00:23.760 --> 00:00:26.810
In this mission, you'll work
through natural selection,

9
00:00:26.860 --> 00:00:28.020
step by step.

10
00:00:28.070 --> 00:00:31.530
You'll weigh up the reasons the
idea was such a hard sell at

11
00:00:31.580 --> 00:00:32.530
the time.

12
00:00:32.580 --> 00:00:34.950
And you'll look at the
evidence for evolution,

13
00:00:35.000 --> 00:00:38.830
from fossils to bacteria
that resist antibiotics.

14
00:00:38.880 --> 00:00:43.150
Your mission: find out why a
big idea took so long to win

15
00:00:43.200 --> 00:00:44.810
scientists over.
